messages:
jane_cust: Hey — running into a weird one. During streaming responses (SSE) our mobile app often drops mid-stream when users switch from WiFi -> cellular. We get a partial output and the client doesn't get a resume token. Happens on iOS 16.4 and Android 13. SDK v0.9.2. Any ideas?

ian_support: Sorry you're hitting that, @jane_cust. Do you have a specific request example or logs? Is the client closing the connection or is it server-side?

jane_cust: We only see it from client logs: socket.onclose with code 1006. On server-side we occasionally see `client disconnected: EOF` in the nginx proxy logs. Example request: streaming chat completions for ~45s. Happens more when network toggles.

liam_sre: 1006 usually means abnormal closure (network drop). Two things to confirm: 1) whether the client attempts reconnect and 2) whether the server supports any resume semantics. Our platform currently doesn't natively resume token-by-token for SSE streams — you have to re-request. Can you repro with curl on a mobile network or with a network flapping tool?

alex_mobile: We can repro reliably on my phone with airplane-mode toggle. Client code uses EventSource (webview) and also native okhttp SSE for android. Both fail with 1006. Client doesn't attempt a smart resume today; it just restarts the request from scratch which means users sometimes lose the partial content.

ian_support: Okay. Short-term we can surface partial outputs to the user as soon as we receive them, and then on reconnect attempt to continue by re-sending the prompt with the last-known partial output as context. Not ideal but a practical workaround.

liam_sre: From infra side, two possible improvements: 1) lower the idle keepalive ping interval on proxies and servers so short network blips don't get treated as long idle; 2) add a lightweight heartbeat SSE event (server -> client) every 15s so mobile carriers/NATs don't drop the TCP connection. Right now proxies might drop after ~60s of silence.

ian_support: @liam_sre can you paste the relevant nginx / proxy settings we should tweak in customer infra or recommend in our docs?

liam_sre: Sure. Example nginx keepalive tweaks we recommend to customers running a reverse proxy in front of SSE endpoints:```http
proxy_read_timeout 90s;  # time nginx waits for a response before closing
proxy_send_timeout 90s;
proxy_buffering off;     # disable buffering for SSE
keepalive_timeout 65s;
```
But note: on some mobile carriers short flaps will still yield 1006 because the TCP connection was reset. Heartbeat events help.

jane_cust: Is there anything we can enable on Redwood side? We saw occasional `stream terminated: idle_timeout` traces in the tenant logs.

liam_sre: We have a server-side idle timeout guard to protect resources; default is 120s. But the real problem here is intermediate network devices dropping long-lived TCP connections during visible silence. For streaming chat you typically want periodic events so that the connection is not idle. We're considering adding an option to emit `:heartbeat` SSE comments on idle.

ian_support: For now, you can implement client-side reconnection logic with exponential backoff and supply the last partial message as a prefix in the new request. Example flow: 1) stream -> receive chunks to UI 2) on close with code 1006, call /session-checkpoint to persist last chunk id (or just store locally) 3) re-open stream and send prompt + last partial chunk as context.

alex_mobile: Example client snippet we use to detect 1006 and restart (pseudo):```js
es.onclose = (e) => {
  if (e.code === 1006) {
    // show "reconnecting" UI
    retryBackoff();
  }
}
function retryBackoff() {
  setTimeout(() => openStream(prefill), nextDelay());
}
```
We can push a patch that stores the last chunk into local DB and replays it into the resumed request.

jane_cust: That should work for us short-term. Any chance the platform could emit an id per chunk so resuming is easier than stuffing partial text into the new prompt?

liam_sre: Good product ask. We could add optional per-chunk metadata (chunk_id / cumulative_token_count) in a small header/event, which would make dedup/resume logic much simpler. I'll open an RFC.

sre-bot: Incident created: INC-2026-451 - Investigate SSE mobile reconnection UX (owner: liam_sre).

ian_support: Filed notes for the customer: recommend client heartbeat + reconnect with prefill. Also suggest they test with proxy settings above and try disabling carrier-level aggressive NAT if possible. I'll schedule a short follow-up call for repro next week.

jane_cust: Thanks everyone — will try the client-side patch and report back with logs. Appreciated! :pray:
